---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout ambient>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#work">skip to work</a>

  <header class="hero" id="top">
    <div class="hero-frame">
      <div class="topbar">
        <p class="site-name">ayaan retiwala <span>· platform engineer</span></p>
        <nav class="hero-nav" aria-label="Page">
          <a href="#work">work</a>
          <a href="#made">made</a>
          <a href="#contact">contact</a>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>i build all<br />the way down.</h1>
        <p>
          at excloud, i built the core of a public cloud, from qemu hosts and spdk
          volumes to the console and cli people used to run it.
        </p>
        <a class="hero-action" href="#work">selected work ↓</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="reading-ground">
    <div class="reading-inner">
      <section class="content-section" id="work">
        <div class="section-label" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>01</span>
          <span>work</span>
        </div>

        <div class="section-body">
          <p class="section-lede">
            i spent three years building excloud's core platform with the engineering lead,
            then operating it for more than 4,000 accounts.
          </p>

          <article class="experience-entry">
            <header class="entry-heading">
              <div>
                <h2>excloud</h2>
                <p class="entry-role">platform engineer</p>
              </div>
              <p class="entry-date">jun 2023 to aug 2026<br />remote</p>
            </header>

            <div class="prose">
              <p>
                my work crossed the whole machine: qemu/kvm compute, spdk block storage,
                managed kubernetes, networking, identity, and the tools people used to control them.
              </p>
              <p>
                it was a small team, so production was part of the design. i handled escalations
                directly and carried what broke back into the control planes.
              </p>
            </div>

            <dl class="work-notes">
              <div>
                <dt>compute / storage</dt>
                <dd>
                  a go control plane over qemu/kvm, and spdk + nvme-of block storage whose
                  reconciler recovered interrupted provisioning instead of leaving orphaned volumes behind.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>clusters / network</dt>
                <dd>
                  managed kubernetes through bootstrap, cilium, csi, and karpenter;
                  plus identity, authoritative dns, and the arp/ndp machinery under the network.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>developer surface</dt>
                <dd>
                  a go http layer that derives openapi 3.1 from types, feeding the sdk, cli,
                  and terraform provider used across more than twenty services.
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>

            <aside class="remembered-bug">
              <p class="aside-label">one bug i remember</p>
              <p>
                a borrowed header outlived its buffer in the kubernetes api transport.
                i traced it through http/2, hpack, and opentelemetry. the fix was about ten lines.
              </p>
            </aside>

            <p class="measurements" aria-label="Excloud at handover">
              <span>4,000+ accounts</span>
              <span>380 active vms</span>
              <span>140 managed postgres clusters</span>
              <span>20+ internal services</span>
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section" id="made">
        <div class="section-label" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>02</span>
          <span>made</span>
        </div>

        <div class="section-body">
          <p class="section-lede">some things i made because i wanted them to exist.</p>

          <div class="project-list">
            <article class="project-row">
              <header>
                <h2>dbconsole</h2>
                <p>electron · postgres</p>
              </header>
              <p>
                a postgres workbench for web and macos, with streaming results, schema graphs,
                destructive-query warnings, and encrypted query sync.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="project-row">
              <header>
                <h2>cbmanager</h2>
                <p>swift · appkit · sqlite</p>
              </header>
              <p>
                a native macos clipboard manager with instant paste-back, ocr for copied images,
                and local search over a sqlite history.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="project-row">
              <header>
                <h2>rig</h2>
                <p>react · fastify · websockets</p>
              </header>
              <p>
                a phone-first console for dispatching <code>pi</code> sessions and watching tool calls
                live while my computer does the work.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="project-row">
              <header>
                <h2>tachyon</h2>
                <p>pwa · offline-first</p>
              </header>
              <p>
                an offline-first manga reader with downloads, auto-scroll, source adapters,
                and anilist sync.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <p class="project-note">
            more finished things and unfinished ideas <a href="https://github.com/lolwierd" rel="noreferrer">live on github.</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="site-footer" id="contact">
        <div>
          <p class="footer-name">ayaan retiwala</p>
          <p>vadodara, india</p>
        </div>

        <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Contact">
          <a href="mailto:me@lolwierd.com">email</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/lolwierd" rel="noreferrer">github</a>
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/lolwierd" rel="noreferrer">linkedin</a>
          <a href="/colophon">colophon</a>
        </nav>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
